    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d388">

                <pb facs="0721" n="625" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg625"/>

                <head>No. 386.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Bassett.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-07-22"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 22,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 207.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi> With reference to your 326 of the 9th
                    instant, acquainting the Department with the honors paid to the United States
                    and to the President, by President Domingue and by the diplomatic
                    representatives at Port au Prince, on the national anniversary of the
                    Independence of the United States, I have to request you, in the name of the
                    President, to convey to President Domingue his acknowledgments for the friendly
                    sentiments toward the United States expressed in his note, a copy of which
                    accompanied your dispatch.</p>
                <p>I am &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
